{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux","id":27226,"title":"Abyssals, New Take [redux]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-10T09:01:31-08:00","id":27226,"title":"Abyssals, New Take [redux]","content":"My first post was a vast jumble, so I decided to redo it, try to make my arguments more clear and valid.<br /> <br /> This is just an exercise. I don't really see anything coming from this.<br /> <hr />Abyssals annoy me. In the wide wonderful world of Exalted, why do we have this one splat that seems convinced in putting up a stock villain? You have three paths with them: Loyalist dark death murderman, anti-\u201chero\u201d murderman (i.e. murder-hobo), and redemptionist \u201cI\u2019m really just a Solar in black makeup.\u201d Why should Abyssals be so restricted? Abyssals <i>are</i> of the Void, Death, and Undeath, they bring that to Creation just by <i>existing</i>; they don\u2019t need some outside mandate to bring that to Creation by an arbitrary Resonance murder count.<br /> <br /> The point of this post is to scrap Abyssals and rebuild them from the ground up, specifically to avoid these problems with current Abyssals, (arguments in spoiler tag):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They\u2019re one dimensional Villains. We need to round them out, let some be healers, musicians, kings, rulers, and true heroes while <i>still</i> being Agents of the Void. (Murder deathspark is still favored, don\u2019t worry.)</li> <li>Their current tie to Solars diminishes the Solar story. A connection between Solars and Abyssals is interesting, but not in \u201chere\u2019s the fallen paladins.\u201d</li> <li>The \u201cdevil\u2019s deal.\u201d Having to agree to be \u201cevil\u201d just reinforces how \u201cevil\u201d Abyssals are. Isn\u2019t it interesting to play someone who didn\u2019t <i>want</i> to gaze into the Abyss?</li> </ol><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>One dimensional villains.</li> </ol>As it currently stands, there\u2019s only three viable paths for Abyssals, all very limited. Hopefully this will change in 3e\u2026but from the kickstarter spoiler, I\u2019m not holding out hope. Basically, you\u2019re either going to be a Loyalist murder villain, an anti-\u201chero\u201d, or a redemptionist. The first works just fine, it\u2019s what they\u2019re tailored around. The redemptionist is a <i>Solar </i>story, not an Abyssal one. You\u2019re a Solar that starts out in black makeup and sheds it. It\u2019s okay as a story, but a heroic Abyssal shouldn\u2019t be forced to be a Solar to be heroic.<br /> That leaves the anti-hero. I\u2019m not a big fan of anti-heroes from the beginning; but the Abyssal version doesn\u2019t even work for me. \u201cI only kill bad people.\u201d Yeah. Sure you do. You\u2019re just a villain pretending to be good. Disagree with me, it is an opinion after all, but even if you do, it\u2019s still a very limited role.<br /> So, basically, you have two workable Abyssal concepts, that are both narrow. This needs to be changed.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The current Solar tie.</li> </ol>The thing I love about Exalted is there is no morality system. Nothing definitely says you\u2019re good or bad. Solars are both the greatest heroes and the worst villains of the system. Or, that\u2019s how it <i>would </i>be if Abyssals weren\u2019t fallen Solars. Oh sure, lore says that the gathering of Solar shards was completely random, but we all know what Abyssals are: fallen paladins, deathknights. Abyssals have the whole \u201credemption\u201d storyline, where they become good again and therefore a <i>Solar.</i><br /> All this starts to draw implicit connections: Abyssals=evil=inverse Solars, therefore Solars must implicitly be good. I know the books try to make it clear this doesn\u2019t happen, but it\u2019s not effective. Western society is still hung up on black and white morality, DnD, and Lord of the Rings. You have to take care when you\u2019re trying to subvert these preconceptions, and unfortunately when you put the Abyssals into the \u201cevil villain\u201d camp (see complaint number 1), you also separate Solars into the \u201cgood hero\u201d camp.<br /> There should be a connection between Solar and Abyssal, but it shouldn\u2019t be a \u201cfallen\u201d Solar type. Rather, it should be a sibling-type, \u201cI can see him in me.\u201d<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The \u201cdevil\u2019s deal.\u201d</li> </ol>Aside from Infernals, no other Exalt type requires you to agree to serve your new God. It just\u2026<i>happens.</i> I don\u2019t like it for Infernals that much either, but it\u2019s not as intrusive there: the Yozi already have some control issues. Aside from the Ebon Dragon, they all have an issue with this whole \u201cfree will\u201d thing, considering how they got stung with it in the past. Even then, all you\u2019re doing is agreeing to serve the Yozi, which in itself doesn\u2019t really have clear goals, and can be interpreted in good or bad light: the Yozi, are neither good nor bad. It\u2019s just a different master, particularly to someone who might find the rule of Yu-Shan unfair.<br /> For the Abyssals, though, you have to agree to destroy the world. If that\u2019s not pure evil, I don\u2019t know what is. That\u2019s not a good start to a well-rounded splat, and just reinforces #1.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> With all that said, here\u2019s my attempt to rework them from the ground up. Because I can, I\u2019m tearing it down to the ground and ignoring all but the core concepts, much like 3e. It\u2019s going to be in a more \u201cdeveloper\u201d voice, and will probably have some holes in it since it\u2019s just an idea. <hr /><br /> <br /> The power of the Sun is so great and well defined, that even his absence takes form and has power of its own: his shadow alone is a mighty God in itself. This glory was likewise passed into his greatest works: his Solar Exaltations. For each Solar that he created and imbued with his power, a shadow of their greatness was also formed; an aspect of darkness, but wonderful and powerful in its own right.<br /> <br /> The Sun was aware of these shadows and cast them into the Void, that empty space that formed when the Primordials created reality out of the Wyld. They were supposed to stay, were it not for the Neverborn and the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn were cast into the Void, and became aware of these shadows of the Solar exalts. However, they could do nothing with them, as beings of unreality they had no power over reality. That changed with the Deathlords. Imbued by the Neverborn with the force of the Void, but containing just enough remnants of Creation, they were the bridge between reality and the Abyss. With the whisperings of the mad Neverborn guiding them, the Deathlords forged these Solar shadows into Exalts of their own rights, forces made from and encapsulating the void\u2014the Abyssals.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal Exaltation is based around the shadow of the Solar Exaltation. Like the Solar, it is guided to those in their moment of greatness. Unlike the Solar, though, this candidate must have a connection to the void. More often than not, this simply means that they are dying. Perhaps their moment of glory was one of self-sacrifice, and the Abyssal Exaltation comes upon them as they lie in a pool of their own blood. But there are other ways. Perhaps the person is void-tainted, or in their heart lies a darkness in itself. It matters not what the connection is, as long as there is something for some seed of Abyss in the candidate.<br /> Another key difference between a Solar Exaltation and an Abyssal Exaltation is that when the Sun chooses his exalts, he can peer into their soul and see if their moment of glory was based upon true heroism or selfish greed. The Neverborn and the Abyssal Exaltation cannot, or rather if they can, they do not care. They will Exalt those regardless of their intentions\u2014heroic or villainous.<br /> <br /> The Abyss in these newly exalted cries out inside their souls. They are driven to fill the void in whatever way they can. Many destroy what they can in rage of the consumption in their soul, but others try to fill it in whatever way they can. Some, even, on looking into the Void within themselves, realize how precious reality is and work to preserve it.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal Exalted were created to be servants and agents of the Deathlords and Neverborn. In theory, that means they are quite restricted and commanded by their \u201csuperiors.\u201d In practice, though, the Abyssals have a great reign in their actions. The Neverborn and Deathlords are often content to just let the agents of the void exist in Creation, for they are confident their Abyssals will bring about the destruction of the world simply by existing and being an anathema to all of reality. Occasionally, though, the Deathlords do attempt to assert their authority over their deathknights, to varying degrees of success.<br /> <br /> \u201cNew\u201d possible concepts.<br /> <br /> The Hedonist.<br /> The Abyssal saw the void, and realized how wonderful reality is. Like a starving man who finds even the simplest bread a glorious meal, this Abyssal revels in everything that reality has to offer. Everything to her is the best possible thing, and they spend their life consuming and trying everything possible to pleasure herself.<br /> <br /> The Musician.<br /> When the air is filled with nothing but music, it blurs together into nothing but meaningless sound. The musician knows how powerful the empty notes are, bringing emphasis to that lone note. They inspire through the love of absence, forcing people to treasure more of what they already have.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:49:45-08:00","id":27357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux#post27226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another key difference between a Solar Exaltation and an Abyssal Exaltation is that when the Sun chooses his exalts, he can peer into their soul and see if their moment of glory was based upon true heroism or selfish greed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? N\u02d0o, that's not how anything works.<br /> The Sun Exalts people based on heroism (that is, greatness) and, possibly, a sense of kinship. Given that he is the usurper king of a derelict Heaven, that means some seriously unpleasant characters are worthy of his blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:52:37-08:00","id":27361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27357#post27357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? N\u02d0o, that's not how anything works.<br /> The Sun Exalts people based on heroism (that is, greatness) and, possibly, a sense of kinship. Given that he is the usurper king of a derelict Heaven, that means some seriously unpleasant characters are worthy of his blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how the 3e exaltation works anymore, so this was my best guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:37:01-08:00","id":27402,"title":"","content":"Hey, I am new here but figured I would speak up because I am a big fan of Abyssals. <br /> <br /> As far as your logic, it is true for 2nd Ed but pretty off as far as Holden's reveals of 3rd Ed according to the &quot;What we know so far..&quot; wiki.<br /> <br /> That said, I really like this idea in theory. I am currently running a game in 2.5 and would love to do this to my players. My big question is how does it change charm sets? With charms like the Melee tree, it can basically stay the same but once an Abyssal frees itself from the Neverborn and possibly redeems to a more purer void. Charms sets like Medicine and Crafts make zero sense. <br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on that and what would you suggest besides just Void flavored Solar charms for replacements? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:43:51-08:00","id":27410,"title":"","content":"Another thought... <br /> <br /> This idea does have the potential to upset a lot of plots. I like that but does throw off the Necro-whale Yozi/Neverborn plan. How did the Neverborn find these Exaltations? Did they somehow resonate with the Jade prison and get sucked in when the Solars were thrown in and thus the Necro-whale grabbed those because them rushed him (void to void). Does it change the number of Infernals too somehow or are those villainous Solars still?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:45:38-08:00","id":27412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux#post27226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><hr />Abyssals annoy me. In the wide wonderful world of Exalted, why do we have this one splat that seems convinced in putting up a stock villain? You have three paths with them: Loyalist dark death murderman, anti-\u201chero\u201d murderman (i.e. murder-hobo), and redemptionist \u201cI\u2019m really just a Solar in black makeup.\u201d Why should Abyssals be so restricted? Abyssals <i>are</i> of the Void, Death, and Undeath, they bring that to Creation just by <i>existing</i>; they don\u2019t need some outside mandate to bring that to Creation by an arbitrary Resonance murder count.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it has gotten slightly better than your first post, you might want to consider the fact that anyone who cares about Abyssals might be thrown off by the tone of your post. It does not come off as a serious invitation to debate when you declare all Abyssals to be &quot;murdermen&quot; or &quot;Solars in black make-up&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:45:44-08:00","id":27414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HokyoRoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27402#post27402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I am new here but figured I would speak up because I am a big fan of Abyssals.<br /> <br /> As far as your logic, it is true for 2nd Ed but pretty off as far as Holden's reveals of 3rd Ed according to the &quot;What we know so far..&quot; wiki.<br /> <br /> That said, I really like this idea in theory. I am currently running a game in 2.5 and would love to do this to my players. My big question is how does it change charm sets? With charms like the Melee tree, it can basically stay the same but once an Abyssal frees itself from the Neverborn and possibly redeems to a more purer void. Charms sets like Medicine and Crafts make zero sense.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on that and what would you suggest besides just Void flavored Solar charms for replacements?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not that great at mechanics. But my suggestion would be to just rebuild them from the ground up.<br /> <br /> Like, a Medicine charm would be that &quot;You banish the broken bone and pain to the void, replacing it with a nothingness. No longer does your arm have any bones in it, but the void itself has become your structure.&quot;<br /> <br /> The easiest way would just be to refluff the charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:55:37-08:00","id":27429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27414#post27414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not that great at mechanics. But my suggestion would be to just rebuild them from the ground up.<br /> <br /> Like, a Medicine charm would be that &quot;You banish the broken bone and pain to the void, replacing it with a nothingness. No longer does your arm have any bones in it, but the void itself has become your structure.&quot;<br /> <br /> The easiest way would just be to refluff the charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our rules AST's had similar thoughts on both counts. <br /> <br /> Another issue that this brings up too is that the number of Celestial Exalts is terrifying. 300 Solar , 300 Abyssals, 100 Sidereals, 100 Nocturnals (if you use them like I do). Not that it is bad but it does potentially fill the &quot;Solars&quot; win feel if not handled well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:57:51-08:00","id":27431,"title":"","content":"You've lost what makes Abyssals interesting in this version. You've cut out the element of self-wrought tragedy that made heroic Abyssals compelling and sympathetic and villianous Abyssals so very damned. You have essentially painted a Solar black and called it an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> A few specific points:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux#post27226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their current tie to Solars diminishes the Solar story. A connection between Solars and Abyssals is interesting, but not in \u201chere\u2019s the fallen paladins.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are not paladins. A Solar can be a paladin, but Solar and paladin are just classifications that overlap. A Sidereal or a Lunar or even an Infernal could be just as much a paladin as any Solar.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are supposed to be reflections of Solars. They are darkness where the Solars are light. Abyssals are cold where Solars are warm. Both are glorious, powerful beyond measure, and immeniently capable. Yes, Abyssals are well described by the word &quot;fallen&quot;, but that is the driving force of an Abyssal's story, the thing that really makes him different than a Solar. An Abyssal is a Solar who has already made a big mistake and will soon be forced to make a choice about it - does he try to rectify the mistake? justify it? How does he live with himself?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The \u201cdevil\u2019s deal.\u201d Having to agree to be \u201cevil\u201d just reinforces how \u201cevil\u201d Abyssals are. Isn\u2019t it interesting to play someone who didn\u2019t <i>want</i> to gaze into the Abyss? </div> </div> </div>Who said all Abyssals <i>want</i> to agree to the deal? The only thing that can be said about Abyssals is that they didn't want to die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing I love about Exalted is there is no morality system. Nothing definitely says you\u2019re good or bad. Solars are both the greatest heroes and the worst villains of the system. Or, that\u2019s how it <i>would </i>be if Abyssals weren\u2019t fallen Solars. Oh sure, lore says that the gathering of Solar shards was completely random, but we all know what Abyssals are: fallen paladins, deathknights. Abyssals have the whole \u201credemption\u201d storyline, where they become good again and therefore a <i>Solar.</i><br /> All this starts to draw implicit connections: Abyssals=evil=inverse Solars, therefore Solars must implicitly be good. I know the books try to make it clear this doesn\u2019t happen, but it\u2019s not effective. Western society is still hung up on black and white morality, DnD, and Lord of the Rings. You have to take care when you\u2019re trying to subvert these preconceptions, and unfortunately when you put the Abyssals into the \u201cevil villain\u201d camp (see complaint number 1), you also separate Solars into the \u201cgood hero\u201d camp.<br /> There should be a connection between Solar and Abyssal, but it shouldn\u2019t be a \u201cfallen\u201d Solar type. Rather, it should be a sibling-type, \u201cI can see him in me.\u201d </div> </div> </div>There's lots of implicit morality words in Exalted. We sling around words like demon, sorcery, holy, bureaucrat, Heaven, Hell, and more on a regular basis. This does not mean that an Abyssal's &quot;redemption&quot; makes him &quot;good&quot;. An Abyssal &quot;redeems&quot; himself when he seeks to not be an Abyssal anymore, just like a Solar can &quot;fall&quot; by agreeing to become an Abyssal, but that doesn't actually attach a moral judgement to the process. An Abyssal could &quot;redeem&quot; himself for purely selfish reasons and a Solar can &quot;fall&quot; to save lives. These might not happen often or be the easiest scenarios, but they are valid scenarios.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the Abyssals, though, you have to agree to destroy the world. If that\u2019s not pure evil, I don\u2019t know what is. That\u2019s not a good start to a well-rounded splat, and just reinforces #1. </div> </div> </div>The only &quot;well rounded&quot; splat in Creation are the Solar Exalted. Every other type of Exalt is biased towards certain stories. It's hard to escape the bureaucracy of Heaven as a Sidereal. It's hard to escape the dynastic politics of the Realm as a Terrestrial. It's hard to escape being used as a tool of murder as an Abyssal. This is as it should be.<br /> <br /> The major objection with Abyssals is not that it is hard to escape being a tool of murder, but that it is too hard. Murder currently defines all that an Abyssal can do instead of being the playground where they start out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another key difference between a Solar Exaltation and an Abyssal Exaltation is that when the Sun chooses his exalts, he can peer into their soul and see if their moment of glory was based upon true heroism or selfish greed. </div> </div> </div>This is wrong. The Unconquered Sun has no power to judge your great deeds as &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil&quot;. He does not weigh the souls of those he Exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hedonist.<br /> The Abyssal saw the void, and realized how wonderful reality is. Like a starving man who finds even the simplest bread a glorious meal, this Abyssal revels in everything that reality has to offer. Everything to her is the best possible thing, and they spend their life consuming and trying everything possible to pleasure herself.<br /> <br /> The Musician.<br /> When the air is filled with nothing but music, it blurs together into nothing but meaningless sound. The musician knows how powerful the empty notes are, bringing emphasis to that lone note. They inspire through the love of absence, forcing people to treasure more of what they already have. </div> </div> </div>How are either of these concepts something that couldn't be done before? I could use both as loyalist Abyssals and the Hedonist as a classic rebel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:06:55-08:00","id":27448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HokyoRoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27410#post27410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thought...<br /> <br /> This idea does have the potential to upset a lot of plots. I like that but does throw off the Necro-whale Yozi/Neverborn plan. How did the Neverborn find these Exaltations? Did they somehow resonate with the Jade prison and get sucked in when the Solars were thrown in and thus the Necro-whale grabbed those because them rushed him (void to void). Does it change the number of Infernals too somehow or are those villainous Solars still?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the Jade Prison is a thing anymore. I'm don't now why the Solars are returning. I got the feeling that the Sun stopped Exalting people for a while because of disappointment, and has now only recently started back up? If not, the Jade Prison breaking could be changed to just all the Yozi's doing for Infernals.<br /> <br /> Also, for the Neverborn finding the Solar Shadows..<br /> 1. They had a lot of time.<br /> 2. When there's <i>something</i> in <i>nothing</i>, it kinda sticks out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it has gotten slightly better than your first post, you might want to consider the fact that anyone who cares about Abyssals might be thrown off by the tone of your post. It does not come off as a serious invitation to debate when you declare all Abyssals to be &quot;murdermen&quot; or &quot;Solars in black make-up&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a post for people who already like Abyssals. They already have what they want.<br /> <br /> Plus...isn't the appeal of Abyssals (if you already like them) that they <i>are</i>\u200b murdermen?<br /> <br /> I dunno. Everytime I hear what people like about Abyssals as they currently stand, I just don't get it. Don't get me wrong, I'm not saying you're wrong for playing them as they currently are (and this writeup still leaves that as the more &quot;default&quot; playstyle of Abyssals--it just explores an option where that's not the <i>only</i> way to play them.) I just find that unpalatable and one-dimensional if that's <i>all</i> they are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:13:38-08:00","id":27458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27448#post27448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure the Jade Prison is a thing anymore. I'm don't now why the Solars are returning. I got the feeling that the Sun stopped Exalting people for a while because of disappointment, and has now only recently started back up? If not, the Jade Prison breaking could be changed to just all the Yozi's doing for Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I'd pretty much guarantee that the Jade Prison is still a thing.<br /> 2. Sol stopped granting Exigence, not Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn't a post for people who already like Abyssals. They already have what they want. </div> </div> </div>No, we didn't. We got most of what we wanted, but we got a crappy Charm set and Resonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus...isn't the appeal of Abyssals (if you already like them) that they <i>are</i>\u200b murdermen? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dunno. Everytime I hear what people like about Abyssals as they currently stand, I just don't get it. Don't get me wrong, I'm not saying you're wrong for playing them as they currently are (and this writeup still leaves that as the more &quot;default&quot; playstyle of Abyssals--it just explores an option where that's not the <i>only</i> way to play them.) I just find that unpalatable and one-dimensional if that's <i>all</i> they are. </div> </div> </div>It's not all they are supposed to be. See Resonance as for why they never became what they could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:14:57-08:00","id":27459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HokyoRoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27429#post27429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Our rules AST's had similar thoughts on both counts.<br /> <br /> Another issue that this brings up too is that the number of Celestial Exalts is terrifying. 300 Solar , 300 Abyssals, 100 Sidereals, 100 Nocturnals (if you use them like I do). Not that it is bad but it does potentially fill the &quot;Solars&quot; win feel if not handled well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically that would be &quot;250 Solars, 50 Infernals, 300 Abyssals...etc.&quot; but yes.<br /> <br /> I've never felt that the numbers should be closely adhered to. So, if you feel there are too many Solars, just make less of them! My standard writeup says that there should be the same number of Abyssals as Solars and Infernals combined, but that can easily be made less if you just say that the Deathlords are still refining the Solar Shadows into more Abyssals. My idea just doesn't allow more Abyssals than Solars and Infernals....which is admittedly a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:24:46-08:00","id":27465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27448#post27448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure the Jade Prison is a thing anymore. I'm don't now why the Solars are returning. I got the feeling that the Sun stopped Exalting people for a while because of disappointment, and has now only recently started back up? If not, the Jade Prison breaking could be changed to just all the Yozi's doing for Infernals.<br /> <br /> Also, for the Neverborn finding the Solar Shadows..<br /> 1. They had a lot of time.<br /> 2. When there's <i>something</i> in <i>nothing</i>, it kinda sticks out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't a post for people who already like Abyssals. They already have what they want.<br /> <br /> Plus...isn't the appeal of Abyssals (if you already like them) that they <i>are</i>\u200b murdermen?<br /> <br /> I dunno. Everytime I hear what people like about Abyssals as they currently stand, I just don't get it. Don't get me wrong, I'm not saying you're wrong for playing them as they currently are (and this writeup still leaves that as the more &quot;default&quot; playstyle of Abyssals--it just explores an option where that's not the <i>only</i> way to play them.) I just find that unpalatable and one-dimensional if that's <i>all</i> they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something feels off in this response. Automatically it reduces the Abyssals and their fans to hack and slash monsters which I know for me is absolutely untrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:29:15-08:00","id":27471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27458#post27458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. I'd pretty much guarantee that the Jade Prison is still a thing.<br /> 2. Sol stopped granting Exigence, not Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, we didn't. We got most of what we wanted, but we got a crappy Charm set and Resonance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not all they are supposed to be. See Resonance as for why they never became what they could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on all points including bad charm sets that there is no reason to take, oppressive resonance, and easy stereotyping. <br /> <br /> One fix I use in my game for redeemed Abyssal is the use of the Resonance system from the Modern setting in Shard. Far better and fits way better with the themes. <br /> <br /> On the note of the Jade Prison, changing this aspect of story would be a massive overhaul in my opinion as it would drastically change the Sidereal, the Usurpation, and the reason the Solar were gone. Never mind that the Sol just not paying attention because of the Xbox of divinity is stupid, but now the world going to shit is directly his fault. Ouch. &gt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:30:40-08:00","id":27472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27431#post27431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've lost what makes Abyssals interesting in this version. You've cut out the element of self-wrought tragedy that made heroic Abyssals compelling and sympathetic and villianous Abyssals so very damned. You have essentially painted a Solar black and called it an Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep typing and erasing what I'm saying. Because you say things that are logical, I just don't agree with the premises.<br /> <br /> I think it's because we disagree on the current state of Abyssals and our ideas of what they should be.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that your Abyssal is all about the tragedy: that they made a bad deal and now have to live with it. That's not what Abyssals are to me: they are Chosen of the Void, whose &quot;creators&quot; want to destroy the world, but are trying to figure out how to fit the Void--unnatural as it is--into Creation. Or, perhaps, if it should. (If not, which is better, the Abyss's consumption, or Creations...creation?)<br /> <hr />Just toss out that whole &quot;Sun looking into the hearts of Solars.&quot; It was a bad way to explain my idea.<br /> <hr />I'm still not sure on the Jade Prison. But if it exists, fine. In my version it's the Yozi who break into it, not the Neverborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:38:30-08:00","id":27480,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I need to clarify something:<br /> <br /> Can there be characters that are Abyssals that are wonderful?<br /> <b>Absolutely</b><br /> <br /> The problem is, in my view, that anything that is not: 1. Outright villain, 2. anti-&quot;hero&quot;, or 3. Redemptionist is outright punished and discouraged by the Abyssal lore and ruleset. You <i>can</i> make an interesting and fully-dimensional character, but you have to fight the splat and rules tooth and nail to do it.<br /> <br /> Any character, regardless of splat, can be full, interesting, and worthwhile. It's just a matter of where the rules and lore point you toward. The Abyssal book, (mainly due to Resonance, yes, but also because of the general tone set and how/who exalts) slaps your hands and punishes you every time you try to avoid killing everything in sight.<br /> <br /> Whenever I'm making generalizations like a &quot;Solar character&quot; or an &quot;Abyssal character,&quot; I'm talking about the stereotype of the splat, and how easy it is to deviate from that stereotype. Abyssals are the most narrow stereotype, as well as the hardest to deviate from that central theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't mix that up with &quot;A character who <i>happens</i> to be an Abyssal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:42:15-08:00","id":27488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27472#post27472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I keep typing and erasing what I'm saying. Because you say things that are logical, I just don't agree with the premises.<br /> <br /> I think it's because we disagree on the current state of Abyssals and our ideas of what they should be.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that your Abyssal is all about the tragedy: that they made a bad deal and now have to live with it. That's not what Abyssals are to me: they are Chosen of the Void, whose &quot;creators&quot; want to destroy the world, but are trying to figure out how to fit the Void--unnatural as it is--into Creation. Or, perhaps, if it should. (If not, which is better, the Abyss's consumption, or Creations...creation?)<br /> <hr />Just toss out that whole &quot;Sun looking into the hearts of Solars.&quot; It was a bad way to explain my idea.<br /> <hr />I'm still not sure on the Jade Prison. But if it exists, fine. In my version it's the Yozi who break into it, not the Neverborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>So then how did they do it because demons have to be summoned and they can't act in Creation without Heaven attacking them? I mean, that is why they needed the Neverborn in the first place. It is fine to change it but it has to make sense and balance with the rest of the story. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like the idea of the change but if it creates this much havoc with the story arches as 2.5 has them set. It creates issues. <br /> <br /> I mean, if we are going to do a massive overhaul to the whole background story. Why not just wait for third? <br /> <br /> The best thing to do in my view is to get REALLY clear on the themes involved and the backstory in its entirety and figure out how to do something like this with the minimal number of changes to the overall story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:50:09-08:00","id":27496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HokyoRoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27488#post27488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So then how did they do it because demons have to be summoned and they can't act in Creation without Heaven attacking them? I mean, that is why they needed the Neverborn in the first place. It is fine to change it but it has to make sense and balance with the rest of the story.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like the idea of the change but if it creates this much havoc with the story arches as 2.5 has them set. It creates issues.<br /> <br /> I mean, if we are going to do a massive overhaul to the whole background story. Why not just wait for third?<br /> <br /> The best thing to do in my view is to get REALLY clear on the themes involved and the backstory in its entirety and figure out how to do something like this with the minimal number of changes to the overall story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, you mistake the point of this post. This isn't a rewrite of the rules for 2.5. This is old man dragonmystic sitting on his porch and crabbing, going &quot;If I were to write Abyssals for 3e, this is what I would do.&quot;<br /> <br /> It really has no point other than that, because I know the Devs are going to go ahead and write them how they want, ignoring my personal preferences (*gasp,* the nerve of not bending to my will! :P )<br /> <br /> Trust me, if this was an actual serious project in the same vein as the Argent Witches Rewrite, I'd put a lot of effort into making sure all the plot holes were neatly tied together and everything made sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:53:50-08:00","id":27503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems to me that your Abyssal is all about the tragedy: that they made a bad deal and now have to live with it. That's not what Abyssals are to me: they are Chosen of the Void, whose &quot;creators&quot; want to destroy the world, but are trying to figure out how to fit the Void--unnatural as it is--into Creation. Or, perhaps, if it should. (If not, which is better, the Abyss's consumption, or Creations...creation?) </div> </div> </div>The problem with making them Chosen of the Void is that the Void is, by design, utterly simplistic. This is great when it's acting as the greatest black hole trash compactor, but not so much when you wanted to draft a Sail Charm (unless you're really fond of &quot;And then kill someone&quot; as an additional cost for every Charm). By making this the central focus, you just hasten the path to making all Abyssals into murdermen/those that are murdermen for great justice/those that fight against being murdermen. This isn't overwhelmingly what Abyssal players like, as seen by all the hate 2E Resonance gets.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm still not sure on the Jade Prison. But if it exists, fine. In my version it's the Yozi who break into it, not the Neverborn. </div> </div> </div>&quot;...And so the remaining Sidereals took the Jade Prison and, after fashioning 108 starmetal hooks from those brethren lost in the Usurpation, anchored it within the Maw of the Void, forever in sight but completely out of reach since none could cross the event horizon of Oblivion. Over the centuries, as the hate and fury of the slain Primordials continually drained into the Void and soaked those Solar shards closest to the Jade Prison's exterior, the very nature of some of the shards began to warp; They retained the nearly boundless power, but what once was light was now dark. Then they were let loose...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":870,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","user":"Side Item","date":". 12-10-2013, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T16:18:38-08:00","id":27605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27472#post27472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep typing and erasing what I'm saying. Because you say things that are logical, I just don't agree with the premises.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing my job then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's because we disagree on the current state of Abyssals and our ideas of what they should be.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that your Abyssal is all about the tragedy: that they made a bad deal and now have to live with it. That's not what Abyssals are to me: they are Chosen of the Void, whose &quot;creators&quot; want to destroy the world, but are trying to figure out how to fit the Void--unnatural as it is--into Creation. Or, perhaps, if it should. (If not, which is better, the Abyss's consumption, or Creations...creation?) </div> </div> </div>What? Abyssals are not and never were Champions of the Void. Second Edition had them drawing upon the Essence of the Void, but that was by way of the Neverborn. They are the Champions of the Neverborn, willing or unwilling. Their narrative has never been about trying to reconcile the Underworld and Creation. Their narrative has always been about &quot;I agreed to be Creation's murder weapon. What do I do about that?&quot;. It has always been a strangely personal story, writ large accross Creation but fought in the Abyssal's heart. How much destruction will he sow before he finds a line he will not cross? Does such a line exist? If they find a line, how do they answer? Do they strive to break their chains? Do they bleed and die for a chance to rejoin Creation as Solars?<br /> <br /> The Abyssal narrative is ultimately an exploration of a character by the harshest acid test possible. After all, real character is who you are in the dark.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/27226-abyssals-new-take-redux?p=27480#post27480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I think I need to clarify something:<br /> <br /> Can there be characters that are Abyssals that are wonderful?<br /> <b>Absolutely</b><br /> <br /> The problem is, in my view, that anything that is not: 1. Outright villain, 2. anti-&quot;hero&quot;, or 3. Redemptionist is outright punished and discouraged by the Abyssal lore and ruleset. You <i>can</i> make an interesting and fully-dimensional character, but you have to fight the splat and rules tooth and nail to do it.<br /> <br /> Any character, regardless of splat, can be full, interesting, and worthwhile. It's just a matter of where the rules and lore point you toward. The Abyssal book, (mainly due to Resonance, yes, but also because of the general tone set and how/who exalts) slaps your hands and punishes you every time you try to avoid killing everything in sight.<br /> <br /> Whenever I'm making generalizations like a &quot;Solar character&quot; or an &quot;Abyssal character,&quot; I'm talking about the stereotype of the splat, and how easy it is to deviate from that stereotype. Abyssals are the most narrow stereotype, as well as the hardest to deviate from that central theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't mix that up with &quot;A character who <i>happens</i> to be an Abyssal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You are half right here. Second Edition Abyssals have the narrowest stereotype and have the hardest time deviating from that central theme. This is not because of a flawed premise, but because the mechanics of Charms and Resonance do not allow for anything but those few narrow stereotypes. The lore ignores options other than servitude and rebellion because they forgot that other options could exist - they aren't disallowed, they just aren't explored.<br /> <br /> If the mechanics of Resonance and Chams didn't force me to muder and kill at every turn, I could perhaps look at being a ghost king or championing the causes of the dead, but doing that using current mechanics just results in pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}